{"id": "de-en-14", "hyp": "Based on the context of a sign above a door in a phone photo, **\"AUSGANC\"** is almost certainly a misspelling or OCR error of **\"AUSGANG\"** (German for \"exit\").  \n\n### Translated Text:  \n**EXIT**  \n\n### Reasoning:  \n- Door signs globally use **\"EXIT\"** or **\"OUT\"** to indicate the way out.  \n- \"AUSGANG\" is a standard German term for \"exit,\" which aligns perfectly with door signage.  \n- OCR errors from phone photos (e.g., poor lighting, angled text) often distort letters—**\"G\"** may have been misread as **\"C\"** (e.g., \"AUSGANG\" → \"AUSGANC\").  \n- No other plausible meaning fits a door sign in this context.  \n\nThis translation ensures clarity and safety for users encountering the sign.", "ms": 1662.4, "tokens": 193}
